// Copyright (c) 2023-2024 Amazon.com, Inc.  All rights reserved.

(module ion_semantic_model "/fusion"
  '''
A denotational semantic model of Ion.

TODO
----
Terminology/Readability:
* The names around "document symbols" don't read well in prose. "local symbols"
  might be better but that requires careful editing to keep "local" precise.
* Figure out the proper name for `I`.  N? Z?
* Less type-switching via E[[]] denotations
  * Easier with distinct typed nulls
    * [LITERALS] Requires literals to render them as typewriter `null.foo`.
* Separate syntactic IVM from semantic spec-version?
* Print the Appendix in manually-assembled sections.
  * Should have a way to detect when a domain element is forgotten.

Features:
* Optional macro names; can streamline some tests
* Implement Decimal, Float, Timestamp, Blob/Clob
* To handle 1.1 composite module symtabs, Module needs SymTok* not Unicode*
* $ion_encoding
  * Aliases would allow better testing without macro-definitions implemented.
    * Requires a MacroMap (MacroBindings?) = Unicode -> Macro
  * Export from.
  * Export by macro reference.  Requires Unicode_split, digit detection/parse.
  * `load` clause with max-id.
    * Unclear how to wire the exact/inexact match and max-id to later clauses.
      * Perhaps add LoadedModule to track that data, and return from ModuleMap.
    * Accept non-exact-match modules in `symbol_table`.
  * `use` clauses at directive-level; more wiring challenges.
  * Accept symbols in `symbol_table` inner lists.
  * Spec says various encoding-directive elements are unannotated, but the
    model doesn't enforce that.
  * Spec should ban the name $ion in load and import.
  * Spec says `symbol_table` rejects duplicate module names, and `$ion`.
    * I'm not sure the duplicate filter achieves anything; the same module can
      still appear under different names, with no difference in outcome.
* [MAC-ID] Macro identity and proper ambiguity detection
* [VALID-NAME] Validate module, macro, and parameter names.
* Eexpr in field-position (struct inlining)
  * If `{(:values {a:1}), b:2}` ==> `{ a:1, b:2 }` then what about `{ {a:1}, b:2 }`?
    Isn't (:values V) == V ?
* Macro argument type-checking

Defects:
* SIDs should be non-negative.
* The spec doesn't say that SST must have its annotation as the first one.
* [SST Semantics] "When mapping from string to symbol ID, there may be multiple
  associated IDs (the same string could appear twice as children of the symbols
  field). Implementations MUST select the lowest known ID, and all other
  associated IDs MUST be handled as if undefined."
  * Not sure what "handled as undefined" implies.
* Catalog construction should reject duplicate keys, so we don't imply anything
  about selection criteria.
* Struct denotations should be order-agnostic. See L.I.S.P. §5.5

Cleanup:
* `lambda`s should instead use `mk_fn` with ad-hoc signature.


Spec Issues: 1.1
----------------
* Spec doesn't describe how ungrouped tagless ZERO_OR_ONE is invoked without a
  value in either Text Eexps or TDL.
* Consider replacing `(retain *)` with just `(retain)`.  It eliminates some
  failure modes and reads nicely.  However, it may be surprisingly inconsistent
  compared to the non-empty behavior.
* Rationalize whether $ion can be in a `macro_table`.
  * Perhaps not a problem in $ion_encoding/macro_table since its version is
    implied.
  * If exported in-full from a shared module, it must be tied to that module's
    spec-version.  Which means diff exports can use diff system-module versions.


Spec Issues: 1.0
----------------
* No mention of possible annotations on imports field or its entries.
* "A version marker can also occur at non-initial positions at the top level,
  and it will have the same effect; when encountered below top-level, it has no
  processing effect and is treated as an ordinary user value."
  * Wrong, IVMs are syntactically distinct and cannot appear elsewhere.
* "Null elements declare undefined symbol IDs (“gaps”) within the sequence;
  implementations must handle requests for such symbols the same as if the
  requested ID beyond the end of the list."
  * BUT: "beyond the end" is an error.
  * AND: what does "requests for such symbols" mean?
* Content under "Imports" should use present/absent instead of defined/undefined
  since the latter has other meaning.
* [Symbol Zero] "$0 is only semantically equivalent to itself and to
  locally-declared SIDs with unknown text."
  * Probably better to treat the local case as something other than "unknown"
    so that term only applies to the SST case.  A local null entry is _known_ to
    be $0, but we know _nothing_ about an absent (or undersized substitute) SST.
  '''


  (require "/fusioncontrib/denotation/dsl")

  (provide (all_defined_out))


  (define_model Ion
    (import B I Unicode)
    (dom 'Unicode?*' = (** 'Unicode?'))


    //=============================
    // Application-layer Data Types

    (dom Value     = (* 'SymTok*'::annots Content::content))
    (dom Content   = (+ Symbol List Sexp Struct NullNull Bool Int String
                        /*Decimal Float Timestamp Blob Clob*/))


    // Simple values require no expansion.
    // Their 'syntax' and 'application' denotations are the same.

    (dom DotNull  = (= DOTNULL) "Sentinel for typed nulls")
    (dom NullNull = (+ DotNull))
    (dom Bool     = (+ B DotNull))
    (dom Int      = (+ I DotNull))
    (dom String   = (+ Unicode DotNull))


    // Symbols

    (dom Sym0      = (= SYM0)            "The undefined symbol $0")
    (dom AbsentSym = (* Unicode::module I::index))
    (dom SymTok    = (+ Unicode Sym0 AbsentSym))
    (dom Symbol    = (+ SymTok DotNull))


    (fn SymTok_matches ((s SymTok) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of s Unicode)
           (U_EQ (lower s Unicode) u)))

    (fn Symbol_matches ((s Symbol) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of s SymTok)
           (SymTok_matches (lower s SymTok) u)))

    (fn Value_is_symbol_matching ((v Value) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
           (Symbol_matches (lower (Value_content v) Symbol) u)))

    (fn 'Value?_is_symbol_matching' ((v 'Value?') (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (opt_is_present v) (Value_is_symbol_matching (opt_value v) u)))


    // Containers

    (dom List     = (+ 'Value*' DotNull))
    (dom Sexp     = (+ 'Value*' DotNull))
    (dom Struct   = (+ 'Field*' DotNull))
    (dom Field    = (* SymTok::name Value::value))


    (fn Value_seqElements ((v Value) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
        (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')
        (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*')))


    (fn Fields_get ((fs 'Field*') (u Unicode) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty fs)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (let [(f (seq_head fs)),
              (vs (Fields_get (seq_tail fs) u))]
          (if (SymTok_matches (Field_name f) u)
            (seq_prepend (Field_value f) vs)
            vs))))

    (fn Struct_get ((s Struct) (u Unicode) -> 'Value*')
      (Fields_get (lower s 'Field*') u))

    (fn Struct_get1 ((s Struct) (u Unicode) -> 'Value?')
      (let [(vs (Struct_get s u))]
        (if (EQ (seq_length vs) 0)
          (opt 'Value?')
          (if (EQ (seq_length vs) 1)
            (opt 'Value?' (ith vs 0))
            (wrong "Repeated field: " u)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Abstract Syntax Trees, which can contain unresolved SIDs

    (dom TSTree     = (+ STree IVM))
    (dom STree      = (+ SValue SEexp))
    (dom SValue     = (* 'SSymTok*'::annots SContent::content))
    (dom SContent   = (+ SSymbol SList SSexp SStruct NullNull Bool Int String
                         /*Decimal Float Timestamp Blob Clob*/))

    (dom SSymTok   = (+ Unicode I))
    (dom SSymbol   = (+ SSymTok DotNull))

    (dom SList     = (+ 'STree*' DotNull))
    (dom SSexp     = (+ 'STree*' DotNull))

    (dom SField    = (* SSymTok::name STree::tree))
    (dom SStruct   = (+ 'SField*' DotNull))

    (dom SEexp      = (* MacroRef::ref 'STree*'::args))
    (dom MacroRef   = (* 'Unicode?'::module NameOrAddr::macro))
    (dom NameOrAddr = (+ Unicode I))


    // Ion Version Markers

    (dom IVM = (* I I) "Ion version markers")

    (const IVM_1_0 (tuple IVM 1 0))
    (const IVM_1_1 (tuple IVM 1 1))

    (fn IVM_eq ((i1 IVM) (i2 IVM)-> B)
      (and (EQ (ith i1 0) (ith i2 0))
           (EQ (ith i1 1) (ith i2 1))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Parsing Interface

    // Here we abstract over the parser, to show the encoding feedback loop.
    // The parsing layer is given a subset of the expansion environment.
    // It would be easier to just pass the Environment, but this is explicit
    // WRT exactly what information can affect parsing.

    (dom ParseStep    = (* TSTree::tree ParseStream::next))
    (dom ParseStream  = (-> IVM 'ParseStep?'))

    (dom Document  = (^ is_truthy) "Ion documents")
    (dom Parser    = (-> Document ParseStream))


    //==========================================================================
    // Expansion of abstract syntax trees into values

    (dom Environment = (* Catalog::catalog
                          Module::sysModule
                          ModuleMap::modules
                          'SymTok*'::docSymbols
                          'Unicode*'::mactab))
    // docSymbols does not include $0 or system symbols


    (fn currentSpecVersion ((r Environment) -> IVM)
      (Module_specVersion (Environment_sysModule r)))

    (fn currentSymtab ((r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (let [(ss (Module_symtab (Environment_sysModule r)))]
        (seq_prepend (lift_to SymTok SYM0)
                     (seq_append (compile_symtab ss "$ion" (seq_length ss))
                                 (Environment_docSymbols r)))))


    (dom ModuleMap = (-> Unicode Module))

    (fn emptyModuleMap ModuleMap (u)
      (wrong "Module not in scope: " u))

    (fn ModuleMap_extend ((mm ModuleMap) (u Unicode) (m Module) -> ModuleMap)
      (mk_fn ModuleMap (u1)
        (if (U_EQ u1 u) m
          (mm u1))))

    (fn currentModuleMap ((r Environment) -> ModuleMap)
      // Adding $ion to the front is defensive, perhaps needlessly so.
      (ModuleMap_extend (Environment_modules r) "$ion" (Environment_sysModule r)))


    (fn expand_STree ((t STree) (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of t SValue)
        (seq 'Value*' (expand_SValue (lower t SValue) r))
        (expand_SEexp (lower t SEexp) r)))

    (fn 'expand_STree*' ((ts 'STree*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty ts)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (seq_append ('expand_STree'  (seq_head ts) r)
                    ('expand_STree*' (seq_tail ts) r))))

    (fn expand_SValue ((sv SValue) (r Environment) -> Value)
      (tuple Value ('expand_SSymTok*' (SValue_annots  sv) r)
                   ('expand_SContent' (SValue_content sv) r)))

    (fn expand_SContent ((sv SContent) (r Environment) -> Content)
      (if (element_of sv SSymbol)
        (lift (expand_SSymbol (lower sv SSymbol) r) Content)
        (if (element_of sv SList)
          (lift (expand_SList (lower sv SList) r) Content)
          (if (element_of sv SSexp)
            (lift (expand_SSexp (lower sv SSexp) r) Content)
            (if (element_of sv SStruct)
              (lift (expand_SStruct (lower sv SStruct) r) Content)
              (if (element_of sv NullNull)
                (lift (lower sv NullNull) Content)
                (if (element_of sv Bool)
                  (lift (lower sv Bool) Content)
                  (if (element_of sv Int)
                    (lift (lower sv Int) Content)
                    (if (element_of sv String)
                      (lift (lower sv String) Content)
                      (wrong "not implemented in this model"))))))))))


    // Symbol expansion

    (fn expand_SSymbol ((v SSymbol) (r Environment) -> Symbol)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Symbol)
        (lift (expand_SSymTok (lower v SSymTok) r) Symbol)))

    (fn expand_SSymTok ((s SSymTok) (r Environment) -> SymTok)
      (if (element_of s Unicode)
        (lift (lower s Unicode) SymTok)
        (let [(i  (lower s I)),
              (ts (currentSymtab r))]
          (if (< i (seq_length ts))
            (ith ts i)
            (wrong "Invalid symbol address " i)))))

    (fn 'expand_SSymTok*' ((ss 'SSymTok*') (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (seq_prepend (expand_SSymTok  (seq_head ss) r)
                     ('expand_SSymTok*' (seq_tail ss) r))))


    // Sequence expansion

    (fn expand_SList ((v SList) (r Environment) -> List)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL List)
        (lift ('expand_STree*' (lower v 'STree*') r) List)))

    (fn expand_SSexp ((v SSexp) (r Environment) -> Sexp)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Sexp)
        (lift ('expand_STree*' (lower v 'STree*') r) Sexp)))


    // Struct expansion

    (fn expand_SStruct ((v SStruct) (r Environment) -> Struct)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Struct)
        (lift ('expand_SField*' (lower v 'SField*') r) Struct)))

    (fn expand_SField ((sf 'SField') (r Environment) -> 'Field*')
      (let [(t  (expand_SSymTok (SField_name sf) r)),
            (vs (expand_STree   (SField_tree sf) r))]
        (letrec [(mk_fields (lambda (vs1)
                              (if (seq_is_empty vs1)
                                  (seq 'Field*')
                                  (seq_prepend (tuple Field t (seq_head vs1))
                                               (mk_fields (seq_tail vs1))))))]
          (mk_fields vs))))

    (fn 'expand_SField*' ((sfs 'SField*') (r Environment) -> 'Field*')
      (if (seq_is_empty sfs)
        (seq 'Field*')
        (seq_append (expand_SField (seq_head sfs) r) ('expand_SField*' (seq_tail sfs) r))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Top-level evaluation

    (dom Evaluator = (-> Document Catalog 'Value*'))

    (fn mk_Evaluator ((p Parser) -> Evaluator)
      (mk_fn Evaluator (d c)
        (let [(p0 (p d)),
              (r0 (tuple Environment c (systemModule IVM_1_0)
                    emptyModuleMap
                    EMPTY_SYMTOKS
                    (seq 'Unicode*' /* No user macros installed */))),
              (k0 (mk_fn TContinuation (r vs) vs))]
          (TE_ParseStream p0 r0 k0))))


    (dom TContinuation = (-> Environment 'Value*' 'Value*')
      "Continuation when expanding top-level values")


    // TODO don't overload p with two different types
    (fn TE_ParseStream ((p ParseStream) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(step (p (currentSpecVersion r)))]
        (if (opt_is_present step)
          (TE_TSTree (ParseStep_tree (opt_value step)) r
            (mk_fn TContinuation (r1 vs1)
              (TE_ParseStream (ParseStep_next (opt_value step)) r1
                (mk_fn TContinuation (r2 vs2)
                  (k r2 (seq_append vs1 vs2))))))
          (k r (seq 'Value*')))))


    (fn TE_TSTree ((t TSTree) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of t IVM)
        (k (compile_IVM (lower t IVM) r) (seq 'Value*'))
        (let [(vs (expand_STree (lower t STree) r))]
          ('TE_Value*' vs r k))))


    (fn TE_Value ((v Value) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (isLocalSymbolTable v)
        (k (compile_LST (lower (Value_content v) Struct) r) (seq 'Value*'))
        (if (and (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_1) (isIonLiteral v))
          (TE_literal v r k)
          (if (and (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_1) (isEncodingDirective v))
            (k (compile_ED (lower (Value_content v) Sexp) r) (seq 'Value*'))
            (k r (seq 'Value*' v))))))

    (fn 'TE_Value*' ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (k r vs)
        (TE_Value (seq_head vs) r
          (mk_fn TContinuation (r1 vs1)
            ('TE_Value*' (seq_tail vs) r1
              (mk_fn TContinuation (r2 vs2)
                (k r2 (seq_append vs1 vs2))))))))


    //==========================================================================
    // IVM compilation

    (fn compile_IVM ((i IVM) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (tuple Environment
        (Environment_catalog r)
        (systemModule i)
        emptyModuleMap
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (seq 'Unicode*' /* No user macros installed */)))


    //==========================================================================
    // $ion_symbol_table compilation

    (fn isLocalSymbolTable ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
                (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_symbol_table"))))

    (fn compile_LST ((s Struct) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (element_of s DotNull)
        (compile_LST (lift (seq 'Field*') Struct) r)
        (let [(is (if ('Value?_is_symbol_matching'
                        ('hint:paren' (Struct_get1 s "imports"))
                        "$ion_symbol_table")
                    (Environment_docSymbols r)
                    (compile_LST_imports (normalize_list (Struct_get1 s "imports")) r))),
              (ss (map 'SymTok*' compile_LST_symbol
                    (normalize_list (Struct_get1 s "symbols"))))]
          (tuple Environment
            (Environment_catalog r)
            (Environment_sysModule r)
            emptyModuleMap
            (seq_append is ss)
            (seq 'Unicode*')))))


    // LST symbols field

    // Try inlining c for better math and collapsing ifs
    (fn normalize_list ((v 'Value?') -> 'Value*')
      (if (opt_is_present v)
        (let [(c (Value_content (opt_value v)))]
          ('hint:oneline'
            (if (and (element_of c List) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
              (lower c List 'Value*')
              (seq 'Value*'))))
        (seq 'Value*')))

    (fn compile_LST_symbol ((v Value) -> SymTok)
      (let [(c (Value_content v))]
        ('hint:oneline'
          (if (and (element_of c String) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
            (lift_to SymTok (lower c String Unicode))
            (lift_to SymTok SYM0)))))

    // LST imports field

    (fn compile_LST_imports ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      // Would be nice to `map`, but this has two args and appends, not cons'es.
      // [FOLD] might do the trick.
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (let [(c (Value_content (seq_head vs)))]
          (let [(ts ('hint:oneline'
                      (if (and (element_of c Struct) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
                        (compile_import (lower c Struct) r)
                        EMPTY_SYMTOKS)))]
            (seq_append ts (compile_LST_imports (seq_tail vs) r))))))

    (fn compile_import ((s Struct) (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (let [(n (normalize_name    (Struct_get1 s "name"   ))),
            (v (normalize_version (Struct_get1 s "version"))),
            (m (normalize_max_id  (Struct_get1 s "max_id" )))]
        (if (or (U_EQ n "")
                (U_EQ n "$ion"))
          (seq 'SymTok*')
          (if (opt_is_present m)
            // We have max_id, find best-match and adjust the length
            (let [(s (bestModule_Catalog (Environment_catalog r) n v))]
              (let [(symtab ('hint:oneline'
                              (if (opt_is_present s)
                                (Module_symtab (SharedModule_module (opt_value s)))
                                (seq 'Unicode?*'))))]
                (compile_symtab symtab n (opt_value m))))
            (let [(s (exactModule_Catalog (Environment_catalog r) n v))]
              (let [(symtab (Module_symtab (SharedModule_module s)))]
                (compile_symtab symtab n (seq_length symtab))))))))


    (fn compile_symtab ((us 'Unicode?*') (moduleName Unicode) (maxId I) -> 'SymTok*')
      (compile_symtab_loop us moduleName maxId 0))

    (fn compile_symtab_loop ((us 'Unicode?*') (moduleName Unicode) (maxId I) (i I) -> 'SymTok*')
      // i = number of elements collected so far; index of next elt
      (if (EQ i maxId)
        (seq 'SymTok*')
        (let [(s (if (and (< i (seq_length us))
                          (opt_is_present (ith us i)))
                   (lift (opt_value (ith us i)) SymTok)
                   (lift (tuple AbsentSym moduleName (+ i 1)) SymTok)))]
          (seq_prepend s (compile_symtab_loop us moduleName maxId (+ i 1))))))


    (fn normalize_name ((v 'Value?') -> Unicode)             // "" = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) String)
                    (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))))
        (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) String Unicode)
        ""))

    (fn normalize_version ((v 'Value?') -> I)                // 1 = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int)
                    (and (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))
                         (>= (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I) 1))))
        (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I)
        1))

    (fn normalize_max_id ((v 'Value?') -> 'I?')              // <> = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int)
                    (and (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))
                         (>= (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I) 0))))
        (opt 'I?' (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I))
        (opt 'I?')))


    //==========================================================================
    // Encoding Modules

    (dom Module        = (* IVM::specVersion 'Unicode?*'::symtab 'ExportedMacro*'::mactab))
    (dom SharedModule  = (* Unicode::name I::version Module::module))


    //==========================================================================
    // Catalogs

    (dom Catalog = (* 'SharedModule*'::modules))


    (fn exactModule_Catalog ((c Catalog) (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule')
      (exactModule_SMs (Catalog_modules c) n v))

    (fn exactModule_SMs ((ss 'SharedModule*') (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        (wrong "No exact-match for " n "@" v)
        (if (and (U_EQ (SharedModule_name (seq_head ss)) n)
                 (EQ (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss)) v))
          (seq_head ss)
          (exactModule_SMs (seq_tail ss) n v))))


    (fn bestModule_Catalog ((c Catalog) (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule?')
      (bestModule_SMs (Catalog_modules c) n v))

    (fn bestModule_SMs ((ss 'SharedModule*') (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule?')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        (opt 'SharedModule?')
        // WARNING These variable names appear in the narrative, keep it in sync!
        (let [(ss1 (bestModule_SMs (seq_tail ss) n v))]
          (if (not (U_EQ (SharedModule_name (seq_head ss)) n))
            ss1
            (if (or (EQ (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss)) v)
                    (not (opt_is_present ss1)))
              // Exact match, or only match.
              (opt 'SharedModule?' (seq_head ss))
              // Inexact match, and the tail had a match.
              (if (or (EQ (SharedModule_version (opt_value ss1)) v)
                      (>  (SharedModule_version (opt_value ss1))
                          (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss))))
                // The tail had an exact match, or larger version.
                ss1
                (opt 'SharedModule?' (seq_head ss))))))))

    (fn Catalog_extend ((c Catalog) (s SharedModule) -> Catalog)
      // TODO reject duplicate key
      (tuple Catalog (seq_prepend s (Catalog_modules c))))


    //==========================================================================
    // System Modules

    (const systemSymbols_1_0
      ('hint:multiline'
        (seq 'Unicode?*'
          (opt 'Unicode?' "$ion")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "$ion_1_0")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "$ion_symbol_table")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "name")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "version")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "imports")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "symbols")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "max_id")
          (opt 'Unicode?' "$ion_shared_symbol_table"))))


    (fn systemModule ((i IVM) -> Module)
      (if (IVM_eq i IVM_1_0)
        (tuple Module i systemSymbols_1_0 (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))
        (if (IVM_eq i IVM_1_1)
          (tuple Module i systemSymbols_1_1 systemMacros_1_1)
          (wrong "Unsupported Ion version: " (ith i 0) "." (ith i 1)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Shared Symbol Table complation

    (fn isSST ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
              (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_shared_symbol_table"))))

    (fn compile_SST ((s Struct) -> SharedModule)
      (let [(n (normalize_name    (Struct_get1 s "name"))),
            // Yes, SST version is normalized to 1
            (v (normalize_version (Struct_get1 s "version")))]
        (if (U_EQ n "")
          (wrong "SST has invalid name")
          (tuple SharedModule n v
            (tuple Module IVM_1_0
              (map 'Unicode?*' compile_SST_symbol
                (normalize_list (Struct_get1 s "symbols")))
              (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))))))


    (fn compile_SST_symbol ((v Value) -> 'Unicode?')
      (let [(c (Value_content v))]
        ('hint:oneline'
          (if (and (element_of c String) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
            (opt 'Unicode?' (lower c String Unicode))
            (opt 'Unicode?')))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Ion 1.1

    //==========================================================================
    // Literals

    (fn isIonLiteral ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
           (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_literal")))

    (fn TE_literal ((v Value) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(v1 (tuple Value (seq_tail (Value_annots v)) (Value_content v)))]
        (if (isLocalSymbolTable v1)
          (wrong "Cannot use literal $ion_symbol_table struct as application data")
          (k r (seq 'Value*' v1)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macros

    (dom Macro = (* Signature::signature Transform::xform))

    (dom Transform = (-> 'Value**' 'Value*'))

    (dom Signature   = (* 'ParamSpec*'::params 'RestSpec?'::rest /* TODO ResultSpec */))

    // TODO Should name be a SymTok?
    (dom ParamSpec   = (* Unicode::name ParamShape::shape))
    (dom RestSpec    = (* Unicode::name  RestShape::shape))

    (dom ParamShape  = (+ SimpleShape GroupShape))
    (dom SimpleShape = (* ParamType::type Cardinality::card))
    // TODO Above works for tagged types; support tagless types
    (dom GroupShape  = (* ParamType::type SeqCardinality::card))
    (dom RestShape   = (* ParamType::type SeqCardinality::card))

    (dom ParamType   = (= ANY))

    (dom Cardinality    = (+ OptCardinality SeqCardinality))
    (dom OptCardinality = (= ZERO_OR_ONE  EXACTLY_ONE))
    (dom SeqCardinality = (= ZERO_OR_MORE ONE_OR_MORE))

    (fn Signature_vars ((s Signature) -> 'Unicode*')
      (seq_append
        (map 'Unicode*' ParamSpec_name (Signature_params s))
        (if (opt_is_present (Signature_rest s))
          (seq 'Unicode*' (RestSpec_name (opt_value (Signature_rest s))))
          (seq 'Unicode*'))))


    (fn is_voidable ((p ParamSpec) -> B)
      (let [(shape (ParamSpec_shape p))]
        (or (and (element_of shape SimpleShape)
                 (is_voidable_Cardinality (SimpleShape_card (lower shape SimpleShape))))
            (and (element_of shape GroupShape)
                 (EQ_Enum (GroupShape_card (lower shape GroupShape)) ZERO_OR_MORE)))))

    (fn is_voidable_Cardinality ((c Cardinality) -> B)
      (or (and (element_of c OptCardinality)
               (EQ_Enum (lower c OptCardinality) ZERO_OR_ONE))
          (and (element_of c SeqCardinality)
               (EQ_Enum (lower c SeqCardinality) ZERO_OR_MORE))))


    (dom ExportedMacro = (* 'Unicode?'::name Macro::macro))


    (fn export ((name Unicode) (params 'ParamSpec*') (rest 'RestSpec?') (xform F) -> ExportedMacro)
      (tuple ExportedMacro (opt 'Unicode?' name)
        (tuple Macro (tuple Signature params rest) xform)))

    (const NO_REST (opt 'RestSpec?'))

    (fn 'param!' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> ParamSpec)
      (tuple ParamSpec name
        (lift_to ParamShape (tuple SimpleShape type (lift_to Cardinality EXACTLY_ONE)))))

    (fn 'group*' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> 'ParamSpec')
      (tuple ParamSpec name
        (lift_to ParamShape (tuple GroupShape type ZERO_OR_MORE))))

    (fn 'rest...' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> 'RestSpec?')
      (opt 'RestSpec?' (tuple RestSpec name (tuple RestShape type ZERO_OR_MORE))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macro Reference Resolution

    (fn resolve_MacroRef ((m MacroRef) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (let [(mod (MacroRef_module m)),
            (mac (MacroRef_macro  m)),
            (mm  (currentModuleMap r))]
        (if (opt_is_present mod)
          // Qualified reference
          (if (element_of mac Unicode)
            (let [(m (resolve_qualifiedName (opt_value mod) (lower_to Unicode mac) mm))]
              (if (opt_is_present m)
                (opt_value m)
                (wrong "No such macro: :" (opt_value mod) ":" (lower_to Unicode mac))))
            (resolve_qualifiedAddr (opt_value mod) (- (lower mac I) 1) mm))
          // Unqualified name or local-offset
          (if (element_of mac Unicode)
            (resolve_unqualifiedName (lower_to Unicode mac) r)
            (resolve_unqualifiedAddr (Environment_mactab r) (- (lower_to I mac) 1) (lower_to I mac) r)))))


    // index is zero-based
    (fn resolve_qualifiedAddr ((u Unicode) (i I) (mm ModuleMap) -> Macro)
      (let [(ms (Module_mactab (mm u)))]
        (if (< i (seq_length ms))
          (ExportedMacro_macro (ith ms i))
          (wrong "Invalid macro address: :" u ":" (+ 1 i)))))

    (fn resolve_qualifiedName ((u1 Unicode) (u2 Unicode) (mm ModuleMap) -> 'Macro?')
      (resolve_ExportedMacros (Module_mactab (mm u1)) u2))

    (fn resolve_ExportedMacros ((ms 'ExportedMacro*') (u Unicode) -> 'Macro?')
      (if (seq_is_empty ms)
        (opt 'Macro?')
        (if (and (opt_is_present  (ExportedMacro_name (seq_head ms)))
                 (U_EQ (opt_value (ExportedMacro_name (seq_head ms))) u))
          (opt 'Macro?' (ExportedMacro_macro (seq_head ms)))
          (resolve_ExportedMacros (seq_tail ms) u))))


    // index is zero-based; i0 is the original value
    (fn resolve_unqualifiedAddr ((ns 'Unicode*') (i I) (i0 I) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (if (seq_is_empty ns)
        (wrong "Invalid macro address: :" i0)
        (let [(ms (Module_mactab ((currentModuleMap r) (seq_head ns))))]
          (if (< i (seq_length ms))
            (ExportedMacro_macro (ith ms i))
            (resolve_unqualifiedAddr (seq_tail ns) (- i (seq_length ms)) i0 r)))))

    (fn resolve_unqualifiedName ((u Unicode) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (let [(ns (seq_prepend (inject_into Unicode "$ion") (Environment_mactab r)))]
        (let [(m (resolve_ModuleNames ns u (currentModuleMap r)))]
          (if (opt_is_present m)
            (opt_value m)
            (wrong "No such macro: :" u)))))

    (fn resolve_ModuleNames ((ms 'Unicode*') (u Unicode) (mm ModuleMap) -> 'Macro?')
      (if (seq_is_empty ms)
        (opt 'Macro?')
        (let [(m1 (resolve_qualifiedName (seq_head ms) u mm)),
              (m2 (resolve_ModuleNames   (seq_tail ms) u mm))]
          (if (opt_is_present m1)
            // TODO [MAC-ID] Compare macro identities to allow benign duplicates.
            (if (opt_is_present m2)
              (wrong "Ambiguous macroreference :" u)
              m1)
            m2))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macro Expansion

    (fn expand_SEexp ((v SEexp) (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_0)
        (wrong "Eexp not allowed in Ion 1.0")
        (let [(m (resolve_MacroRef (SEexp_ref v) r))]
          (Macro_invoke m (SEexp_args v) r))))


    (dom 'Value**' = (** 'Value*'))

    (fn collateArgs ((ps 'ParamSpec*') (rest 'RestSpec?') (r Environment) (ts 'STree*') -> 'Value**')
      (if (seq_is_empty ps)
        (if (opt_is_present rest)
          // We have a rest-parameter, so grab everything that remains.
          (let [(vs ('expand_STree*' ts r)),
                (t (RestShape_type (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest)))),
                (c (RestShape_card (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest))))]
            (seq 'Value**' (validateShape t (lift c Cardinality) vs)))
          (if (seq_is_empty ts)
            (seq 'Value**')                 // All done!
            (wrong "Too many arguments")))
        (let [(p (seq_head ps))]
          (if (seq_is_empty ts)
            // We hava a param, but no more arguments; param must be voidable.
            (if (is_voidable p)
              (seq_prepend (seq 'Value*')
                (collateArgs (seq_tail ps) rest r ts))
              (wrong "Too few arguments"))
            // We have both a param and more arguments
            (let [(t  (seq_head ts)),
                  (is (collateArgs (seq_tail ps) rest r (seq_tail ts)))]
              (if (element_of (ParamSpec_shape p) GroupShape)
                (if (and (element_of t SValue)  // not an Eexp
                         (element_of (SValue_content (lower t SValue)) SList))
                  // TODO reject null.list and annotations
                  (let [(ts1 (lower (SValue_content (lower t SValue)) SList 'STree*'))]
                    // TODO Arity checking of expanded group
                    (seq_prepend ('expand_STree*' ts1 r) is))
                  (wrong "Expected grouping list"))
                // Non-grouped argument expected
                (let [(vs (expand_STree t r)),
                      (t (SimpleShape_type (lower (ParamSpec_shape p) SimpleShape))),
                      (c (SimpleShape_card (lower (ParamSpec_shape p) SimpleShape)))]
                  (seq_prepend (validateShape t c vs) is))))))))

    (fn validateShape ((t ParamType) (c Cardinality) (vs 'Value*') -> 'Value*')
      // TODO type
      (if (element_of c OptCardinality)
        (if (> (seq_length vs) 1)
          (wrong "More than one value provided for parameter")
          (if (and (EQ_Enum (lower c OptCardinality) EXACTLY_ONE)
                   (EQ (seq_length vs) 0))
            (wrong "No value provided for parameter")
            vs))
        (if (and (EQ_Enum (lower c SeqCardinality) ONE_OR_MORE)
                 (EQ (seq_length vs) 0))
          (wrong "No value provided for parameter")
          // ZERO_OR_MORE is handled implicitly; it always passes.
          vs)))

    // Collate, validate the arguments based on the Macro's signature, then
    // invoke the macro
    (fn Macro_invoke ((m Macro) (ts 'STree*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(f (Macro_xform     m)),
            (s (Macro_signature m))]
        (f (collateArgs (Signature_params s) (Signature_rest s) r ts))))


    //==========================================================================
    // $ion_encoding compilation

    (fn isEncodingDirective ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
                (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_encoding"))))

    (fn compile_ED ((s Sexp) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      // TODO Consider disallowing null.sexp
      (if (element_of s DotNull)
        (compile_ED_retain (seq 'Value*')     r)
        (compile_ED_retain (lower s 'Value*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_retain ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) -> Environment)
      // TODO This is inconsistent with other cases where $ion isn't present
      //   ATM we only need it as a way to determine the specVersion.
      (let [(mm0 (ModuleMap_extend emptyModuleMap "$ion" (Environment_sysModule r)))]
        (if (nextClauseIs vs "retain")
          (let [(args (clauseBody (seq_head vs))),
                (mm0  (Environment_modules r))]
            (if (and (EQ (seq_length args) 1)
                     (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head args) "*"))
              (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs) mm0 r)
              // TODO [FOLD]
              (letrec [(retain (|vs1 mm| (if (seq_is_empty vs1)
                                           mm
                                           (retain (seq_tail vs1)
                                             (ModuleMap_extend mm
                                               (Value_symtext (seq_head vs1))
                                               (mm0 (Value_symtext (seq_head vs1))))))))]
                (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs) (retain args mm0) r))))
          (compile_ED_modules vs mm0 r))))

    (fn compile_ED_modules ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "load")
        (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs)
          (compile_ED_load (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail (Environment_catalog r))
          r)
        (if (nextClauseIs vs "module")
          (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs)
            (compile_ED_module (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail (Environment_catalog r))
            r)
          // End of module-decls
          (compile_ED_symtab vs avail r))))

    // Same logic should be used for modules
    (fn compile_ED_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "symbol_table")
        (compile_ED_mactab (seq_tail vs) avail
          (compile_module_symtab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail)
          r)
        (compile_ED_mactab vs avail (seq 'SymTok*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_mactab ((vs 'Value*')
                           (avail ModuleMap)
                           (ts 'SymTok*')
                           (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "macro_table")
        (compile_ED_final (seq_tail vs) avail ts
          (compile_ED_mactab_body (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail)
          r)
        (compile_ED_final vs avail ts (seq 'Unicode*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_final ((vs 'Value*')
                          (avail ModuleMap)
                          (ts 'SymTok*')
                          (us 'Unicode*')
                          (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (not (seq_is_empty vs))
        (wrong "Unexpected encoding clause: " (seq_head vs))
        (tuple Environment
          (Environment_catalog r)
          (Environment_sysModule r)
          avail
          ts
          us)))


    (fn Value_strtext ((v Value) -> Unicode)  (lower (Value_content v) String Unicode))
    (fn Value_symtext ((v Value) -> Unicode)  (lower (Value_content v) Symbol SymTok Unicode))
    (fn Value_int     ((v Value) -> I      )  (lower (Value_content v) Int I))


    // $ion_encoding load

    // TODO Rename; this is also used by inner modules.
    (fn compile_ED_load ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> ModuleMap)
      (let [(name    (Value_symtext (ith vs 0))),   // TODO validate module name
            (catname (Value_strtext (ith vs 1))),
            (version (Value_int     (ith vs 2)))
            // TODO maxid
            // TODO ensure no extra arguments
           ]
        (ModuleMap_extend avail name
          (SharedModule_module (exactModule_Catalog c catname version)))))


    // $ion_encoding module

    (fn compile_ED_module ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> ModuleMap)
      (let [(name (Value_symtext (ith vs 0)))]      // TODO validate module name
        (ModuleMap_extend avail name
          (compile_IM_body (seq_tail vs) avail c))))


    // $ion_encoding symbol_table

    (fn compile_module_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'SymTok*')
        (seq_append (compile_module_symtab_elt (seq_head vs) avail)
          (compile_module_symtab (seq_tail vs) avail))))

    (fn compile_module_symtab_elt ((v Value) (avail ModuleMap) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        // TODO copied from compile_import
        // TODO this assumes exact match acquired
        (let [(symtab (Module_symtab (avail (Value_symtext v))))]
          // Convert Module's Unicode* to SymTok*
          // FIXME This uses the defined name, not the catalog name.
          // Absent-symbol equality is therefore incorrect.
          (compile_symtab symtab (Value_symtext v) (seq_length symtab)))
        (map 'SymTok*' compile_module_symtab_text
          (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*'))))

    (fn compile_module_symtab_text ((v Value) -> SymTok)
      // TODO typecheck, nullcheck
      (lift_to SymTok (Value_strtext v)))


    (fn compile_ED_mactab_body ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) -> 'Unicode*')
      // TODO Use `map`
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'Unicode*')
        // TODO check presence in avail.
        (seq_prepend (Value_symtext (seq_head vs))
          (compile_ED_mactab_body (seq_tail vs) avail))))


    (fn nextClauseIs ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (not (seq_is_empty vs))
           (isClause (seq_head vs) u)))

    (fn isClause ((v Value) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
        // TODO Null check
        (and (not (seq_is_empty (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')))
          (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')) u))))

    (fn clauseBody ((v Value) -> 'Value*')
      (seq_tail (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')))


    //==========================================================================
    // Inline module compilation

    (fn compile_IM_body ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> Module)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "load")
        // Recurse to find more dependencies
        (compile_IM_body (seq_tail vs)
          (compile_ED_load (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail c)
          c)
        // No more dependencies
        (compile_IM_symtab vs avail)))

    (fn compile_IM_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) -> Module)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "symbol_table")
        (compile_IM_mactab (seq_tail vs) avail
          // TODO This doesn't handle absent symbols or their equality.
          (compile_module_symtab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail))
        (compile_IM_mactab vs avail (seq 'SymTok*'))))

    (fn compile_IM_mactab ((vs 'Value*')
                           (avail ModuleMap)
                           (ts 'SymTok*') -> Module)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "macro_table")
        (compile_IM_final (seq_tail vs) avail ts
          (compile_module_mactab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail (seq 'ExportedMacro*')))
        (compile_IM_final vs avail ts (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))))

    (fn compile_IM_final ((vs 'Value*')
                          (avail ModuleMap)
                          (ts 'SymTok*')
                          (ms 'ExportedMacro*') -> Module)
      (if (not (seq_is_empty vs))
        (wrong "Unexpected clause in module: " (seq_head vs))
        (tuple Module
          (Module_specVersion (avail "$ion"))
          (map 'Unicode?*' (|t| (opt 'Unicode?' (lower t Unicode))) ts)
          ms)))


    (fn compile_module_mactab ((vs   'Value*')
                               (mods ModuleMap)
                               (macs 'ExportedMacro*') -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        macs
        (compile_module_mactab (seq_tail vs) mods
          (compile_IM_mactab_elt (seq_head vs) mods macs))))

    (fn compile_IM_mactab_elt ((v    Value)
                               (mods ModuleMap)
                               (macs 'ExportedMacro*') -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      (if (isClause v "macro")
        (compile_macro_defn (clauseBody v) mods macs)
        (let [(mod (mods (Value_symtext v)))]
          (seq_append macs (Module_mactab mod)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Signature compilation

    (fn compile_Signature ((v Value) -> Signature)
      (compile_Signature_params (Value_seqElements v)))

    (fn compile_Signature_params ((ps 'Value*') -> Signature)
      (if (seq_is_empty ps)
        (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*') NO_REST)
        (if (seq_is_empty (seq_tail ps))
          // Last entry, so it can be a rest-spec
          (if (isRestSpec (seq_head ps))
            (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*') (opt 'RestSpec?' (compile_restSpec (seq_head ps))))
            (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*' (compile_paramSpec (seq_head ps))) NO_REST))
          // ELSE there are >1 entries to handle, head cannot be rest-spec
          (let [(s (compile_Signature_params (seq_tail ps)))]
            (tuple Signature
              (seq_prepend (compile_paramSpec (seq_head ps)) (Signature_params s))
              (Signature_rest s))))))

    (fn isRestSpec ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
        (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
          (and (> (seq_length vs) 1)
            (or (Value_is_symbol_matching (ith vs 1) "...")
                (Value_is_symbol_matching (ith vs 1) "...+"))))))

    (fn compile_paramSpec ((v Value) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        (compile_paramType (seq 'Value*') (compile_paramName v))
        (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
          (compile_paramType (seq_tail vs) (compile_paramName (seq_head vs))))))

    (fn compile_paramType ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) -> ParamSpec)
      // TODO type
      (compile_cardinality vs u ANY))

    (fn compile_cardinality ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (finishParamSpec vs u t (lift EXACTLY_ONE Cardinality))
        (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "!")
          (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift EXACTLY_ONE Cardinality))
          (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "?")
            (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ZERO_OR_ONE Cardinality))
            (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "+")
              (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ONE_OR_MORE Cardinality))
              (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "*")
                (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ZERO_OR_MORE Cardinality))
                (wrong "Unexpected element in param-spec: " (seq_head vs))))))))

    (fn finishParamSpec ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) (c Cardinality) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (tuple ParamSpec u
          (lift_to ParamShape (tuple SimpleShape t c)))
        (wrong "Unexpected element in param-spec: " (seq_head vs))))


    (fn compile_restSpec ((v Value) -> RestSpec)
      (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
        (compile_restType (seq_tail vs) (compile_paramName (seq_head vs)))))

    (fn compile_restType ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) -> RestSpec)
      // TODO type
      (compile_restCard vs u ANY))

    (fn compile_restCard ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) -> RestSpec)
      (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "...")
        (finishRestSpec (seq_tail vs) u t ZERO_OR_MORE)
        (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "...+")
          (finishRestSpec (seq_tail vs) u t ONE_OR_MORE)
          (wrong "Unexpected element in rest-spec: " (seq_head vs)))))

    (fn finishRestSpec ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) (c SeqCardinality) -> RestSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (tuple RestSpec u (tuple RestShape t c))
        (wrong "Unexpected element in rest-spec: " (seq_head vs))))


    (fn compile_paramName ((v Value) -> Unicode)
      // TODO [VALID-NAME]
      (lower (Value_content v) Symbol SymTok Unicode))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macro definition compilation

    (dom IEnv = (-> Unicode 'Value*'))
    (dom Interpreter = (-> IEnv 'Value*'))


    (fn compile_macro_defn ((vs   'Value*')
                            (mods ModuleMap)
                            (macs 'ExportedMacro*') -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      // TODO arity check
      (let [(name  (Value_symtext (ith vs 0))),   // TODO [VALID-NAME]
            (sig   (compile_Signature (ith vs 1)))]
        (seq_prepend
          (tuple ExportedMacro (opt 'Unicode?' name)
            (tuple Macro sig (compile_xform (ith vs 2) sig)))
          macs)))

    (fn compile_xform ((v Value) (s Signature) -> F)
      // These functions are invoked after arity checking and grouping, so we
      // can assume the correct number of args (per the Signature) are given.
      (let [(i (interp_template v (Signature_vars s)))]
        // [LET] is not strict on its bound values, so we must explicitly check
        // for, and propagate, compile-time failures.
        (if (is_bottom i)
          i
          (mk_fn Transform (args)
            (let [(e ('IEnv_extend*' emptyIEnv (Signature_vars s)  args))]
              (i e))))))

    // We assume all parameter names are unique

    (fn emptyIEnv IEnv (u)
      (wrong "Unbound variable: " u))

    (fn IEnv_extend ((e IEnv) (u Unicode) (v 'Value*') -> IEnv)
      (mk_fn IEnv (u1)
        (if (U_EQ u u1) v (e u1))))

    (fn 'IEnv_extend*' ((e IEnv) (us 'Unicode*') (vs 'Value**') -> IEnv)
      (if (seq_is_empty us)
        e
        (IEnv_extend ('IEnv_extend*' e (seq_tail us) (seq_tail vs))
          (seq_head us) (seq_head vs))))



    (fn interp_template ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      // These functions are invoked after arity checking and grouping applied.
      // We can assume the correct number of groups (per the Signature) are given.
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        (interp_ref v scope)
        (if (element_of (Value_content v) List)
          (interp_list v scope)
          (if (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
            (wrong "Struct quasi-literals not implemented")
            (if (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
              (interp_sexp v scope)
              (interp_literal v))))))

    (fn 'interp_template*' ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') -> 'Interpreter*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'Interpreter*')
        (seq_prepend (interp_template    (seq_head vs) scope)
                     ('interp_template*' (seq_tail vs) scope))))


    (fn interp_literal ((v Value) -> Interpreter)
      (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
        (seq 'Value*' v)))

    (fn interp_ref ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (let [(u (Value_symtext v))]  // Rejects $0, null, unknown
       (if (seq_is_empty scope)
         (wrong "Unbound variable: " u)
         (if (U_EQ (seq_head scope) u)
           (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
             (env u))
           (interp_ref v (seq_tail scope))))))


    (fn interp_list ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (let [(us (Value_annots v)),
            (is ('interp_template*' (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*') scope))]
        (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
          (letrec [(combine (lambda (is1)                              // [FOLD]
                              (if (seq_is_empty is1) (seq 'Value*')
                                (seq_append ((seq_head is1) env)
                                            (combine (seq_tail is1))))))]
            (seq 'Value*' (tuple Value us (lift (combine is) List Content)))))))

    (fn interp_sexp ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (if (isClause v "literal")
        (interpSF_literal (clauseBody v) scope)
        (wrong "Malformed template: " v)))


    // Special forms

    (fn interpSF_literal ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (if (EQ (seq_length vs) 1)
        (mk_fn Interpreter (env) (seq 'Value*' (seq_head vs)))
        (wrong "Malformed literal clause")))


    //==========================================================================
    // System Module 1.1

    (const systemSymbols_1_1
      (seq_append systemSymbols_1_0
        (seq 'Unicode?*'
          (opt 'Unicode?' "$ion_literal")
          /* ... */)))

    (const systemMacros_1_1
      ('hint:multiline'
        (seq 'ExportedMacro*'
          (export "void"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (rest)
              (seq 'Value*')))
          (export "values"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (ith args 0)))
          (export "make_string"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "content" ANY)                     // TODO should be TEXT
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift (appendText (ith args 0)) String Content)))))
          (export "make_symbol"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "content" ANY)                     // TODO should be TEXT
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift (appendText (ith args 0)) SymTok Symbol Content)))))
          (export "make_list"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift_to Content (lift_to List (ith args 0)))))))
          (export "make_sexp"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift_to Content (lift_to Sexp (ith args 0)))))))
          (export "annotate"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*'
              ('group*' "anns"  ANY)                      // TODO should be TEXT
              ('param!' "value" ANY))
            (opt 'RestSpec?')
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (let [(ts (map 'SymTok*'
                            (lambda (v) // Value -> SymTok
                              (let [(c (Value_content v))]
                                (if (element_of c Symbol)
                                  (if (element_of c Unicode)
                                    (lower c Symbol SymTok)
                                    (wrong ":$ion:annotate doesn't accept null.symbol"))
                                  (if (element_of c String)
                                    (if (element_of c Unicode)
                                      (lift (lower c String Unicode) SymTok)
                                      (wrong ":$ion:annotate doesn't accept null.string"))
                                    (wrong "Not a text value")))))
                            (ith args 0)))]
                (seq 'Value*'
                  (tuple Value
                    (seq_append ts (Value_annots (seq_head (ith args 1))))
                    (Value_content (seq_head (ith args 1))))))))
          /* ... */)))


    (fn appendText ((vs 'Value*') -> Unicode)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (inject_into Unicode "")
        (Unicode_append (Value_unicode (seq_head vs))
          (appendText (seq_tail vs)))))

    (fn Value_unicode ((v Value) -> Unicode)
      (let [(c (Value_content v))]
        (if (element_of c Symbol)
          (if (element_of c Unicode)
            (lower c Symbol SymTok Unicode)
            "")
          (if (element_of c String)
            (if (element_of c Unicode)
              (lower c String Unicode)
              "")
            (wrong "Not a text value")))))
  )

  (define EMPTY_SYMTOKS    (seq 'SymTok*'))
)
